                <pb facs="0288" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3894: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-02T16:00:00+01:00">February 2, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. In public session just concluded, called at request of British Delegation,
                    the Council resumed consideration of the Sino-Japanese dispute.</p>
                <p>[Here follows a report of the meeting; for minutes, see League of Nations, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Official Journal</hi>, March 1932, pages 350–353. The
                    British representative reported on the concerted action being taken by Great
                    Britain and the United States in making representations at Tokyo and Nanking and
                    stated that his Government was satisfied that this action would “receive the
                    approval and support of their colleagues.”]</p>
                <p>8. The meeting closed with the following statement by the President: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“At the conclusion of this meeting I desire to make two statements: First
                            of all, with regard to local events, the Council is bound to await the
                            report of the committee which has been set up at the request of the
                            Council and for which a credit has just been voted; secondly, as regards
                            the general object of this meeting, the proposal of the British
                            representative has been supported by representatives of several other
                            countries. The object of the proposal is to associate the authority of
                            the Council with the steps that have been taken by the different
                            countries for a pacific settlement of this question. Having accorded
                            that authority I hereby declare the meeting closed.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
